  "S7_codes_data analysis.zip": {
    "S7_codes_data analysis/Stress/README.md": "Code to Perform moving window average filter on the measured normal stress raw data\n\nContents:\n* `stress_filter.m` Matlab function to perform moving window average filter, extracting the mean normal stress component and fluctuating stress component.\n\nUse:\n* Update definitions of string `IMF-223`, `-mat` and variables `t` and `p` in `stress_filter.m`, to input the data for analysis.\n* Update definitions of variables `L` and `m`in `stress_filter.m` to select a reasonable window size and cycle index.\n* From Matlab, run `stress_filter.m`",
    "S7_codes_data analysis/Stress/stress_filter.m": "clc\r\nclear\r\n% MOVING AVERAGE FILTER Perform moving window average filter on the\r\n% measured normal stress raw data\r\n\r\n%% Input raw data\r\n% Test No.and data format\r\nload('IMF223','-mat'); \r\n% Time t and replicate test No. g3\r\nt=g3(:,1);\r\n% Measured normal stress p\r\np=g3(:,2);\r\nfs=1/(t(2)-t(1));\r\n\r\n% Half the window size\r\nL=10;  \r\n% Cycle index\r\nm=30;  \r\n% Number of normal stress value\r\nn=length(p);\r\nb=ones(1,L);\r\n% Mean normal stress pa\r\npa=[b*p(1),p',b*p(n)];\r\nb=pa;\r\n\r\n% The moving window averge calculation of pa based on the cycle index\r\nfor k=1:m\r\n    for j=1+L:n+L\r\n        b(j)=mean(pa(j-L:j+L));\r\n    end\r\n    pa=b;\r\nend\r\n\r\n%Calculating the fluctuating stress pf\r\npf=p(1:n)'-pa(1+L:n+L); \r\n\r\n% Plot the raw data, fluctuating stress component, and mean stress\r\n% component\r\nplot(t,p,':',t,pf,t,pa(1+L:n+L),'-.');\r\nxlabel('Time (s)');\r\nylabel('Stress (Pa)');\r\nlegend('Raw data','Fluctuating normal stress','Mean normal stress');\r\ngrid on;"
  }
